Z||000004||Nashco||04-14-2001||01:55 PM||||I agree with Tina, the e-brake handle does look pretty "old school" and could be drastically improved.  I am more into fabricating my own parts, but it would be nice to maybe find an easier alternative.<P>Maybe we should talk to Rodney Dickman about this if we don't know of anything available aftermarket.  He seems to have good resources and already has the customer base to sell more than a few.  My e-brake doesn't work right now, as I haven't had time to fix it since I got my car recently, but I am planning on looking at the e-brake handle while I'm at it to see what can be done.  I can't imagine it's too much different than other hand-brakes and might have similar measurements to other cars.<P>If anybody's done or seen a different e-brake used, let us know...we need to start somewhere <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
